10: joins vs includes?
ans- joins is mainly used to perform SQL joins and filter records based on associated tables, while includes is used to eager load associations and prevent N+1 query problems.


joins ka main purpose SQL JOIN karke filtering/query karna hai.

Example:

User.joins(:posts).where(posts: { status: "published" })

Conceptually SQL:

SELECT users.*
FROM users
INNER JOIN posts ON posts.user_id = users.id
WHERE posts.status = 'published';

⚠️ joins associated records ko automatically memory mein load nahi karta.

2. includes

includes ka main purpose N+1 query problem avoid karna hai.

includes associated records ko preload/eager load karke memory mein available kar deta hai, taaki baad mein user.posts karne par separate query na chale.

users = User.includes(:posts)

users.each do |user|
  puts user.posts
end

Rails associated posts ko efficiently load karne ke liye additional query(s) use kar sakta hai.

Conceptually:

SELECT * FROM users;

SELECT * FROM posts
WHERE user_id IN (1, 2, 3);




11: preload vs eager_load?
ans - Haan, ye includes ke andar ke 2 loading strategies samajh lo:

1. preload

preload separate SQL queries chalata hai.

users = User.preload(:posts)

Roughly:

SELECT * FROM users;

SELECT * FROM posts
WHERE user_id IN (1, 2, 3);

Yaani:

Query 1 → Users
Query 2 → Posts

Important: preload associated table par filtering nahi kar sakta in the same way as a JOIN.

2. eager_load

eager_load LEFT OUTER JOIN use karta hai.

users = User.eager_load(:posts)

Roughly:

SELECT users.*, posts.*
FROM users
LEFT OUTER JOIN posts
ON posts.user_id = users.id;

Yaani:

Users + Posts
      ↓
LEFT OUTER JOIN
      ↓
Single SQL query

Iska benefit ye hai ki associated table ke columns par condition laga sakte ho:

User.eager_load(:posts)
    .where(posts: { status: "published" })
    
    
preload vs eager_load


preload	                				eager_load
Separate queries	        				JOIN query
Usually 2+ queries	        				Usually 1 SQL query
Association preload karta hai   				Association eager load karta hai
JOIN-based filtering ke liye suitable nahi			Associated table par filtering possible
IN (...) query							LEFT OUTER JOIN


Easy trick 🧠	
preload
   ↓
Separate Queries

eager_load
   ↓
LEFT OUTER JOIN
⭐ Interview answer

preload loads associations using separate queries, whereas eager_load uses a LEFT OUTER JOIN to load the main records and associations together.

